 ## Approach
-- E1 reuses the script's atomic-write + KV idioms; the only new primitive is the awk key-rewrite, which preserves the canonical state shape by construction (vs. recomposing from scratch). Disk-before-memory ordering and the `CLEARED` / `SEEDED` contracts keep the determinism-critical sequencing inside bash while the in-memory clear (7.6) stays with the orchestrator. Malformed-state exits always emit the promised machine key first so orchestrator branches stay deterministic.
-- E2 is a standalone wrapper with rooted helpers and session-env rehydration; `write-final-report.sh` stays the pure renderer. One intentional behavior delta: the wrapper drops `--print-stdout`, so the report body appears once at top chat (the orchestrator's authoritative verbatim emit) instead of also in the collapsible Bash stdout. `write-final-report.sh` writes `summary-final.md` regardless of `--print-stdout` (verified), so body content is unaffected; `EMIT_BODY` is additionally gated on successful render and non-empty body so NEVER #20 cannot fire on stale/empty output. Flag both deltas for the review panel.
